[center][font=Arial][size=6][color=#FCEE0A][b]CONFLICT STUDIO[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[color=#00F0FF]Archive and code conflict inspection for Cyberpunk 2077[/color]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/00-overview.gif[/img]
[/center]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ CREDIT FIRST[/b][/color][/size][/font]

[font=Arial]Conflict Studio was inspired by [b]rfuzzo's[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/11126]Archive Conflict Checker[/url]. Please endorse the original tool. Conflict Studio is a separate implementation and does not copy its code or assets.[/font]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ BETA[/b][/color][/size][/font]

[font=Arial]This is a beta. Keep a backup and read the preview before changing archive order. Conflict Studio creates and verifies its own backup, but it cannot decide whether two mods are compatible just because they touch the same file or method.[/font]

[font=Arial]The application is unsigned and self-contained. Windows may show an unknown-publisher warning. Download it only from this page and compare the included SHA-256 checksum if you want to verify the file.[/font]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ WHAT IT DOES[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[list]
[*][font=Arial]Reads the active MO2 or Vortex profile, or a manually selected game folder.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Shows archive winners, losers, identical files, and unresolved order problems.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Finds loose files installed by more than one active mod.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Inspects RedScript methods, CET callbacks, TweakXL changes, REDmods, and ArchiveXL manifests.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Previews archive-order changes before Apply.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Backs up and verifies modlist.txt, rescans, and offers Undo.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Exports a privacy-filtered support report.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/01-overview.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/04-archive-expanded.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/05-code-overview.png[/img]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ VORTEX[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[list=1]
[*][font=Arial]Switch Vortex to advanced mode and open Extensions.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Drop the downloaded ZIP onto the extension installer.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Restart Vortex, activate your Cyberpunk profile, and deploy it.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Launch Conflict Studio from Cyberpunk 2077 → Tools.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/11-vortex-extensions-navigation.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/12-vortex-extension-enabled.png[/img]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ MOD ORGANIZER 2[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[list=1]
[*][font=Arial]Extract the ZIP outside the instance's mods folder.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Add Conflict Studio\ConflictStudio.exe to MO2's executable list.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Set Start in to the folder containing ModOrganizer.ini.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Use [b]--manager mo2 --profile current[/b] as the arguments.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Add ConflictStudio.exe to Settings → Workarounds → Executables Blacklist.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/08-mo2-tool-setup.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qcargile/Cyberpunk-Conflict-Studio/main/docs/nexus/media/10-mo2-blacklist.png[/img]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ IMPORTANT[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[list]
[*][font=Arial]Do not scan the same game through MO2 while Vortex files are deployed. Purge Vortex first or use the Vortex profile.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Cyberpunk must be closed before archive-order writes.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]Conflict Studio does not merge archives, generate patches, or automatically sort mods.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]A shared method or record is a place to inspect, not proof that two mods are incompatible.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[font=Arial]The first large-profile scan can take several minutes. Later scans reuse cached archive fingerprints. If something looks wrong, reproduce it once and copy the report from the Support tab.[/font]
[line]

[font=Arial][size=5][color=#FCEE0A][b]▍ REQUIREMENTS[/b][/color][/size][/font]
[list]
[*][font=Arial]Windows 10 version 2004 or newer, 64-bit.[/font][/*]
[*][font=Arial]A Cyberpunk 2077 installation or active MO2/Vortex profile.[/font][/*]
[/list]

[font=Arial]No separate .NET installation or Cyberpunk framework dependency is required.[/font]
